---
title: Freezer-Friendly Chicken and Rice Casserole
source: claude
servings: 8
tags: [freezer, casserole]
prep time: 20 minutes
cook time: 40 minutes
---

> The milk-free, mozzarella version. Bakes in a 9x13 dish, or in two 8x8 pans for easier freezing.

Boil @long-grain white rice{1.5%cups}(uncooked) in a #pot{} of salted water for about ~{8%minutes}, until still firm in the center. Drain; it finishes cooking in the oven.

Melt @butter{1%tbsp} in a #large skillet{} over medium-high heat. Season @chicken thigh{1.5%lb}(boneless, skinless, cut into 3/4-inch pieces; breast also works) with a little salt and pepper and cook until just browned, about ~{4%minutes}. It doesn't need to cook through. Set aside.

In the same skillet, melt @butter{3%tbsp}. Cook @onion{1}(medium, diced) and @mushroom{8%oz}(sliced) for ~{6%minutes}. Add @garlic{3%cloves}(minced) for 30 seconds, then stir in @flour{5%tbsp}(all-purpose) and cook ~{1%minute}. Slowly whisk in @chicken broth{4%cups}, then add @dried thyme{1%tsp}, @salt{1.5%tsp} and @black pepper{1/2%tsp}. Simmer ~{5%minutes}, until it is thick enough to coat a spoon. Mozzarella is mild, so taste now and add a pinch more salt, garlic or thyme if it seems flat.

Stir the rice, chicken, @broccoli{2%cups}(florets, raw) and 1 cup of the @?mozzarella{2%cups}(low-moisture, shredded, divided) into the sauce. It should look quite saucy, since the rice soaks up liquid as it bakes and freezes.

Transfer to a #9x13-inch baking dish{} and top with the remaining 1 cup of mozzarella.

To bake now: cover with foil and bake at 375°F for ~{30%minutes}. Uncover and bake ~{10%minutes} (10–15) more, until bubbly. Mozzarella browns less than cheddar, so broil the top for 1–2 minutes for color.

> To freeze: cool completely first, then wrap tightly in plastic wrap and foil. Or line the pan with foil, freeze, then lift out the block and wrap it to free up the dish. Label with the date; keeps up to 3 months.

> To reheat: thawed overnight in the fridge, bake covered at 350°F for 40–45 minutes. From frozen, bake covered at 350°F for about 75 minutes, then uncovered for 10–15 more, until it reaches 165°F inside. If it looks dry, stir in a few tablespoons of broth.

> Use block mozzarella you shred yourself if you can; it melts better. Avoid fresh mozzarella, which is too watery for freezing. A couple of tablespoons of grated parmesan, or a splash of cream or a spoonful of cream cheese, adds flavor and richness. Frozen peas and carrots work in place of the broccoli.
